<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka's 96 provisional trade gap down 12.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka's 96 provisional trade gap down 12.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's provisional trade gap for the whole of 1996 fell 12.6 percent to $1.31 billion against $1.5 billion in the previous year, the Central Bank said on Monday.</p>
<p>It said provisional imports in 1996 were $5.417 billion, up two percent over 1995 while exports were $4.10 billion, up eight percent over the previous year.</p>
</text>
